    "textSnapshot": "Problem: The CLI infrastructure had multiple defects preventing reliable command parsing and causing poor resource usage and user experience. Help detection failed to distinguish help requests from data shaped like flags. The explain command buffered unbounded build output into memory, risking OOM on verbose failures. Error resolution was purely shape-based and could not disambiguate common names like Config across packages. Path parsing for the -- separator ignored flag values, so diff --repo -- failed even though -- was a valid directory name. Partial file parse failures silently vanished from user-facing output. Markdown tables corrupted when filenames contained | characters. Multiline shell invocations in documentation guides were validated line-by-line, missing flags on continuation lines.\nSolution: Reimplemented help detection to respect the command's flag-value contracts and the -- separator, so search --query --help is a search for the text, not a help request. Converted explain to streaming input with piped echo, eliminating the memory buffering. Added file and type extraction from error lines to rank ambiguous symbols by context\u2014the error line now disambiguates Config by package. Fixed -- separator parsing to skip value-taking flags. Exposed partial file parse failures by name in index text output instead of silently dropping them. Added Markdown cell escaping to prevent | in filenames from splitting table rows. Enhanced guide validation to join shell-continuation lines before parsing, catching flags on wrapped invocations. Capped the scanned-names dedup set to prevent unbounded growth on broken builds.",
